   "subject": "Changing the plot/image height in rmd",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\">I need to increase the height of the plot/image generated by knitr\r\nwith the rmd file (not save the file with dev). I can’t find whether ggplot2\r\nprovides a mechanism to adjust the image size. Any ideas? <u></u><u></u></p></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "zqz3LnVcBQAJ",
   "from": "Sherif Soliman",
   "author": "98fc74ba56643c44",
   "date": "2016-07-27T18:03:21Z",
   "subject": "Re: Changing the plot/image height in rmd",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div><div style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><div style=\"white-space:normal\">\r\n<p dir=\"auto\">On 27 Jul 2016, at 13:26, Frank wrote:</p>\r\n\r\n<p dir=\"auto\"></p></div>\r\n<div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\"><blockquote style=\"border-left:2px solid #777;color:#777;margin:0 0 5px;padding-left:5px\"><div dir=\"auto\">I need to increase the height of the plot/image generated by knitr with the rmd file (not save the file with dev). I can’t find whether ggplot2 provides a mechanism to adjust the image size. Any ideas?\r\n</div></blockquote></div>\r\n</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div><div style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><div style=\"white-space:normal\">\r\n\r\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hi Frank,</p>\r\n\r\n<p dir=\"auto\">You can see an example of how to do that here:</p>\r\n\r\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://rstudio.github.io/dygraphs/r-markdown.html\" style=\"color:#3983c4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://rstudio.github.io/dygraphs/r-markdown.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792367796483000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2pgXfu8lomvLDY3G5xj6fa\">https://rstudio.github.io/dygraphs/r-markdown.html</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p dir=\"auto\">The link is for a certain plotting package (dygraphs), but the instructions work for any plot in rmarkdown documents.</p>\r\n\r\n<p dir=\"auto\">You can set default <code style=\"background-color:#f7f7f7;border-radius:3px;margin:0;padding:0 0.4em\" bgcolor=\"#F7F7F7\">fig_width</code> and <code style=\"background-color:#f7f7f7;border-radius:3px;margin:0;padding:0 0.4em\" bgcolor=\"#F7F7F7\">fig_height</code> values for the entire rmd document:</p>\r\n\r\n<pre style=\"background-color:#f7f7f7;border-radius:5px 5px 5px 5px;margin-left:15px;margin-right:15px;max-width:90vw;overflow-x:auto;padding:5px\" bgcolor=\"#F7F7F7\"><code style=\"background-color:#f7f7f7;border-radius:3px;margin:0;padding:0\" bgcolor=\"#F7F7F7\">---\r\ntitle: &quot;My Document&quot;\r\noutput:\r\n  html_document:\r\n    fig_width: 6\r\n    fig_height: 4\r\n---\r\n</code></pre>\r\n\r\n<p dir=\"auto\">or set them for specific chunks.</p>\r\n\r\n<pre style=\"background-color:#f7f7f7;border-radius:5px 5px 5px 5px;margin-left:15px;margin-right:15px;max-width:90vw;overflow-x:auto;padding:5px\" bgcolor=\"#F7F7F7\"><code style=\"background-color:#f7f7f7;border-radius:3px;margin:0;padding:0\" bgcolor=\"#F7F7F7\">```{r, fig.width=8, fig.height=4}\r\nggplot(...)\r\n```\r\n</code></pre>\r\n\r\n<p dir=\"auto\">Does this answer your question?</p>\r\n\r\n<p dir=\"auto\">Sherif</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "7MPT7wRdBQAJ",
